<title>USA: Option Care acquisitions to boost revenue.</title>
<headline>Option Care acquisitions to boost revenue.</headline>
<dateline>BANNOCKBURN, Ill. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Option Care Inc said Monday it acquired the assets of two of its largest franchises, a move it said is expected to add more than $12 million in annual revenues.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The assets acquired were Home Pharmacy Inc of Miami, Fla. and Specialized Alternative Care Inc in Ann Arbor, Mich. In conjunction with the Miami transaction, the company also acquired assets of Home Hospital Supply Inc.</p>
<p>President Erick Hanson said these key acquisitions are the first of several planned for 1997.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
